WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.450
Here is how SLIC works.

00:00:01.530 --> 00:00:09.235
The setting is an inverse problem with additive
noise: an observation equals a deterministic signal model plus noise.

00:00:09.315 --> 00:00:15.090
Learn the score of the noise distribution and you
can build the score of the likelihood.

00:00:15.170 --> 00:00:21.344
So they train a score-based diffusion model on real
LIGO noise using denoising score matching,

00:00:21.424 --> 00:00:27.731
then chain it with the Jacobian of a differentiable
IMRPhenomD waveform from the ripple package.

00:00:27.811 --> 00:00:31.790
Sampling uses a Metropolis-adjusted Langevin
algorithm, MALA.
